From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayi <3363523343@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:10:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(osdrv/wifi): support bidirectional BF01 host integration

[description ]:
- Deliver the complete SDIO driver support for the BF01 host/Wi-Fi protocol
  as one feature, including the fixes required while integrating it.
- Receive 0x083B indications through a bounded local ioctl queue and handle
  0x003B Direct Buffer replies with explicit length and allocation limits.
- Restore mismatched SDIO bus width during probe and synchronize startup
  reception with firmware readiness instead of dropping four packets.
- Preserve the module's TCP port filters when opening the host interface,
  adding only the required ICMP/ARP/DNS flags and propagating failures.
- Keep the driver bound while a background worker retries the real WSM
  startup handshake: a 1000 ms indication wait and 1000 ms between cleaned-up
  failed attempts. Publish wlan0 and control readiness only after success.
- Bound startup I/O failures, unwind per-attempt resources, expose startup
  state in sysfs and cancel the worker safely during removal.

[root   cause]:
- The original driver does not expose unsolicited host protocol messages
  and assumes generic fixed-size replies for Direct Buffer exchanges.
- A stale card bus width and fixed startup packet discards can prevent
  enumeration or discard the firmware startup indication.
- Host interface startup overwrites module-owned TCP port filters with
  a port-5001 default, disrupting the module's existing cloud connections.
- A one-shot probe can time out before the module sends its WSM startup
  indication, leaving no wlan0 or control backend even after the module is
  ready; nested startup bus retries also delay the next handshake attempt.

[JIRA      ID]:N/A (BF01 integration)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Applies after the existing BSP osdrv patch series through 0020.
- Requires the paired IPCamera production service for protocol handling.
- Receive queue capacity is 16 messages, each at most 1600 bytes; a full
  queue drops the new indication and emits a rate-limited warning.
- Current host-to-module Direct Buffer JSON limit is 1595 bytes; oversized
  requests are rejected rather than truncated.
- The startup retry path is limited to Linux RHEA SDIO builds; normal I/O
  retry behavior after firmware readiness remains unchanged.
- Replace the previous 0042 and replay from a clean SDK baseline; do not
  apply this complete feature patch on top of an already-applied old 0042.
- Does not change module firmware, pinmux, memory layout or AI/capture policy.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :atbm6461_wifi_sdio.ko
